==============================================================================
Third-party software and services
==============================================================================

This repository contains **no third-party source code and redistributes no
third-party binaries**. Every component below is downloaded from its official
release page at deploy time; see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md section 2.

- AstrBot (https://github.com/AstrBotDevs/AstrBot)
  The bot framework: LLM providers, plugins, platform adapters, WebUI.
  Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0).
  Why used: it is the bot brain this stack deploys. Because it is AGPL, this
  repository must not vendor its code or ship a modified build.

- AstrBot Launcher (https://github.com/AstrBotDevs/astrbot-launcher)
  Desktop launcher that installs AstrBot into an isolated directory, manages
  instances and their Python runtime, and stays in the system tray.
  Licensed under the MIT License.
  Why used: it isolates the Python environment per instance, so the bot does
  not depend on (or pollute) the machine's system Python.

- NapCatQQ (https://github.com/NapNeko/NapCatQQ)
  The QQ protocol side: runs on top of QQ NT and exposes OneBot 11.
  Licensed under a **custom "Limited Redistribution License"** (non-commercial;
  redistribution allowed only with the full license text and clear attribution;
  modified builds may not be published).
  Why used: it is the only maintained way to bridge QQ to OneBot 11.
  This repository therefore never bundles, patches, or republishes it.

- workbuddy2api (https://github.com/linguo2625469/workbuddy2api-panel)
  A multi-account gateway that turns Tencent WorkBuddy accounts into an
  OpenAI-compatible API. Built from source into `wb2api.exe`.
  Licensed under the MIT License (original project by Sliverkiss).
  Why used: it is the model gateway this stack points AstrBot at.

- astrbot_plugin_parser (https://github.com/Zhalslar/astrbot_plugin_parser)
  Optional AstrBot plugin that parses Bilibili / Douyin / Kuaishou /
  Xiaohongshu links and QQ mini-app cards, downloads media and renders cards.
  Licensed under the MIT License.
  Why used: it is the media parser behind `qqbotstack_guard.parse_share_link`.
  Installed from the AstrBot plugin market at deploy time; never vendored here.

- astrbot_plugin_music (https://github.com/Zhalslar/astrbot_plugin_music)
  Optional AstrBot plugin that searches music sources and sends QQ music cards.
  Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0).
  Why used: it provides the `play_song_by_name` LLM tool for natural-language
  song requests. It is installed as an **external plugin** and is not vendored;
  if you redistribute a modified copy, GPL-3.0 obligations apply to that copy.

- ffmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org/)
  Optional portable build used to merge Bilibili DASH audio/video streams and
  transcode AAC profiles. Not redistributed here; download it from the official
  build page at deploy time. License depends on the build (LGPL/GPL).

- QQ NT (https://im.qq.com/)
  Tencent's QQ client. Installed by the NapCat one-key package; no Tencent code
  is redistributed here.

- Go / Python / Node.js
  Toolchains used to build or run the components above. Not redistributed.

==============================================================================
Credentials
==============================================================================

This repository stores **no credentials**. WorkBuddy access tokens live in
`runtime/workbuddy/auths/`, the gateway API key lives in
`runtime/workbuddy/config.json`, and both are excluded by `.gitignore`.
QQ login state is held by QQ NT itself.

See docs/SECRETS.md for the location index.
